{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: bbi-faq-jsonld
  Purpose: Renders a single FAQPage JSON-LD block from a list of "Question||Answer"
           strings. Shared across sub-collection pages (ds-cs-base) and review
           pages (Step 6). The visible FAQ accordion MUST be built from the same
           list, split on the same "||" delimiter, with no divergent text
           transforms, so the schema text byte-matches the on-page Q/A text
           (SCHEMA-CRIT-1).
  Usage (render is sandboxed — build the list with {% assign %} first, then pass
  the plain variable; render does NOT apply filters to argument values, same
  convention as bbi-breadcrumb-jsonld):
    {%- assign faq_items = collection.metafields.faq.items.value -%}
    {%- render 'bbi-faq-jsonld', faq_items: faq_items -%}
  Notes:
    - Each list entry is "Question||Answer". Entries missing "||" are skipped
      (malformed). Question = part before "||", Answer = part after.
    - HONESTY RULE (SCHEMA-CRIT-1c): emits NOTHING if faq_items is blank or yields
      zero valid pairs — never an empty FAQPage.
    - No URLs in this schema, so no absolute-URL handling needed.
    - Strings serialized via `| json`. No `strip` / smart-quote / truncation here:
      the visible accordion splits the SAME source identically, so any transform
      added here must be mirrored there or the byte-match breaks.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign _faq_valid = '' | split: ','
  unless faq_items == blank
    for _entry in faq_items
      if _entry contains '||'
        assign _one = _entry | split: '~~|~~'
        assign _faq_valid = _faq_valid | concat: _one
      endif
    endfor
  endunless
-%}
{%- if _faq_valid.size > 0 -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for _entry in _faq_valid -%}
      {%- assign _parts = _entry | split: '||' -%}
      {%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ _parts[0] | json }},
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": {{ _parts[1] | json }}
      }
    }
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}
